# Track what you wrote, ignore the rest
# Two questions decide every file: can the code recreate it? is it private?
# If yes to either, ignore it. Check why a file is ignored with:
#   git check-ignore -v <file>

## Private or personal

### Secrets
.Renviron
*.key
*.pem

### R session files
.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

### OS files (macOS, Windows)
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.icloud
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

## Recreated by the code

### Data
# Raw and processed data stay out of git (size, licences, reproducibility:
# processed data is regenerated by scripts/). Only the folder READMEs are kept.
# Small reference tables you want to share: add them with a "!" negation here,
# e.g. !data/raw/site_coordinates.csv
data/raw/**
!data/raw/README.md
data/processed/**
!data/processed/README.md

### Outputs
# Figures and tables are regenerated by scripts/. Ignored by default.
outputs/**
!outputs/README.md

### Rendered and temporary files
*_cache/
*_files/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md
.quarto/
*.log
/*.html
*.tmp

### renv
# renv ignores its own internals (renv/library, renv/local, ...) through
# renv/.gitignore once renv::init() has run. Do NOT add renv/ here:
# renv.lock and renv/activate.R MUST be tracked.
